Error: Cannot access refs during render

React refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).

/Volumes/Mastermind 2/agent-workspaces/terminal/web/portfolio-target-feedback-20261022/terminal/components/settings/SectionPortfolioTargets.tsx:69:7
  67 |   // accuracy / usage panels use, so a sign-out or account switch leaves no
  68 |   // row from another owner visible.
> 69 |   if (lastLoadedOwner.current !== null && lastLoadedOwner.current !== ownerKey) {
     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render
  70 |     lastLoadedOwner.current = null;
  71 |     if (state.kind === "loaded") setState({ kind: "idle" });
  72 |   }

